ed red tract  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm on cross section  it is located directly behind the nipple and running from anterior to posterior   In retrospect  this represented fresh hemorrhage rather than biopsy tract   On re examination of the specimen  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm biopsy site is identified 1cm from the anterior margin  Central to this site but in the same general region of breast is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm second biopsy site which includes a clip and is 1 2cm from the posterior deep margin  Surrounding this biopsy site is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm suspicious micronodular region which is 0 6cm from the anterior margin  there is suspicious firm tissue around this site near the deep margin  Approximately 2cm central to this second biopsy site is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm suspicious micronodular region located at the disk edge  which abuts the anterior margin and is 0 4cm from the deep margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of needle tract including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Needle tract including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of needle tract including skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area surrounding needle tract including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue including needle tract   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue including anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue surrounding area of needle tract   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue away from needle tract on medial side   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue away from needle tract on lateral side   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue  Sections submitted after re examination of the specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First biopsy site  including anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Suspicious micronodular tissue with anterior margin next to second biopsy site  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second biopsy site with suspicious tissue next to de