characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue which has a surfacing REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm previously blue dyed tan skin ellipse along the anterior aspect  a single suture designating superior  a triple suture designating medial  and a localizing wire in place  The specimen is black inked along the superior  blue inked along the inferior  red inked along the deep aspect  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm poorly delineated tan white focally hemorrhagic mass 1 0cm from the superior anterior  1 5cm from the medial  1 8cm from the inferior  2 0cm from the lateral and 3 0cm from the deep margins  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue with minimal thin  white  fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial to lateral as follows  A  Medial most margin  B  Adipose tissue adjacent to lesion to include superior and inferior margin  C  Tumor to inferior margin  D  Tumor toward anterior margin  E  Fibrous tissue to superior margin  F  Tumor to anterior superior margin  G  Tumor to anterior inferior margin  H  Lateral most margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  hot and blue left sentinel node  are 2 tan yellow adipose tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The smaller portion contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm