Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 16 CLINICAL DATA  History of left breast carcinoma  status post reconstruction                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  APOCRINE TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  APOCRINE TYPE INVOLVING A MACROCYST  HIGH GRADE  ARISING IN ASSOCIATION WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast tissue with needle  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm white tan mass with a 1 0cm central cystic area  A representative section of tumor is frozen as fx 1 and saved frozen  The remaining tumor is submitted in cassettes A D with additional representative sections of normal breast in cassette E F  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITH APOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 29 CLINICAL DATA  32 year old who had a right breast biopsy which showed a grade 3 invasive ductal carcinoma extending to a margin of the specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST  DEEP  MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  THREE DUCT PROFILES  SPANNING A REGION THAT IS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  MEASURED FROM SLIDES   EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY SITE  WITH ONE FOCUS THAT IS REMOVED_DATE CM FROM A DEEP MARGIN  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  Specimen  1 consists of a breast biopsy with an adherent skin ellipse  The biopsy measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Within the skin ellipse is a healing surgical incisional scar  1 5cm in length  The specimen has been oriented as stated on the container  long suture lateral  and short suture  superior  The specimen has been painted in the following manner  Lateral margin green Medial margin blue Anterior and deep surgical resection margins   black ink  The specimen has been sectioned at 0 5cm intervals and reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  A portion of the biopsy cavity closest to the deep surgical resection margin shows a small focus  0 5 x 0 5cm   of firm  tan tissue suspicious for carcinoma  This area is located 1 2cm from the nearest deep inked surgical resection margin  The biopsy cavity is continuous with the overlying adherent skin ellipse and healing surgical scar  The biopsy cavity comes to within 1 5cm of the medial inked margin and 1 8cm from the lateral inked surgical resection margin  The skin ellipse shows unremarkable tan  wrinkled tissue with no other abnormalities other than the surgical incision  Sections from this specimen will be submitted as follows  A  medial inked surgical resection margins  blue  B  lateral surgical resection margins  green  C  superior surgical resection margins  black  D G  sections through a biopsy cavity  DandE  show closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin                     A shows biopsy cavity in closest approximation to overlying skin ellipse   H  representative section through firm area of breast near medial surgical resection margin  grossly not tumor The second specimen consists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Lymph nodes are identified within this specimen  The largest lymph node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections of the nodes will be submitted in the following cassettes  I  representative sections from 3 nodes J  5 nodes K  5 nodes L  3 nodes M  3 nodes N  nodes Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Ruth B Felsen  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT    report_end  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 17 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 0 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  2  MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  Greater than 95 per cent of the tumor is infiltrating  foci of in situ carcinoma apart from the main tumor are not identified  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The inked margins are negative for tumor  The gross intraoperative impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 6 x 3 x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with accompanying x ray and wire in place  Specimen inked and bisected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  gray nodule suspcious for carcinoma  Surrounded by fat  not present at margin  Nodule too small for other assays  No frozen done  Discussed with surgeon  Section Code  A B  nodule  C D  nodule  E F  margin  G J  margin  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
