y  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm portion of breast tissue with a suture designating the area closest to the nipple  The specimen is inked black and double inked blue at the suture  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hard tan stellate mass within 0 2cm from the inked margin and 1 5cm from the suture  Note that the surgeon looked at the margins in the frozen section lab and looked at the margin  The mass is submitted in cassettes A and B  A representative section of the surrounding tissue are submitted in cassettes C   F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture designating the area farthest from the needle localization specimen towards nipple  The entire specimen is inked black  and the sutured area green  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions  The parenchyma is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes G   L  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS   CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY 