Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 01 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATIED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  40    MIXED MICROPAPILLARY  AND CRIBRIFORM TYPE  3  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SEPARATE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  4  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  6  SIMPLE DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  7  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCYSTS  FIBROSIS  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  8  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma measures 1 5cm in greatest diameter  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The infiltrating lobular carcinoma is separate from the infiltrating ductal carcinoma and measures 0 2cm in diameter  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of pink tan fibroadipose tissue with a firm center and an area  1 5cm   of white tan gritty tissue adjacent to margin  Representative section taken as FX 1  submitted in P and the remainder of the specimen A through O  Sections L and M are adjacent to FX 1  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INVASIVE AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  M  Priscilla Short  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS , Positive.
