e in situ tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  NOTE  The sections stained for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not contain invasive tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 40 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a short suture designating the superior aspect and a long suture designating the lateral aspect  There is an overlying tan white skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm with an eccentrically located unremarkable nipple with no scar grossly appreciated  No axillary tail identified  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm firm to rubbery ill defined area containing a few cystic structures averaging 0 2cm in diameter and containing a friable thick tan white material  This area is located within the upper outer quadrant coming to 1 7cm from the blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 3 5cm from the posterior  Located 2 0cm inferior to the ill defined fibrotic area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined rubbery lobulated slightly indurated fibrotic area which comes to 3 0cm from the inferior blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 2 0cm from the posterior margin  The parenchyma in between these two ill defined slightly indurated fibrotic areas consist of rubbery