ctive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two parts  Labeled  Left breast  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white firm nodule 1cm in greatest dimension  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  now N  The remainder of this specimen is submitted entirely in A through J  with the nodule in A through C  Labeled  Left breast  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 2cm fimr tan nodule  The specimen is submitted entirely in K through M  with the nodule in K  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT   1 EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT   2 EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS LESION IS TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A   1 LEFT BREAST PART B   2 LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
