Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 32 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer which is negative for ER and PR and indeterminate for Her 2neu by FISH and IHC  A CT PET scan is only positive in the breast  She is undergoing planning for adjuvant therapy  A repeat Her 2 neu with FISH is requested on the core biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  Sections of the core biopsy reveal an invasive tumor growing in sheets and large nests of tumor cells with associated desmoplasia  No tubule formation is present  A dense lymphoid infiltrate is also noted  There is only a small portion of normal uninvolved breast parenchyma present at one edge of the core biopsy  The tumor cells are large with abundant ill defined cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  Mitotic figures  including atypical forms are readily identified  The morphologic findings are those of a poorly differentiated carcinoma and in the context of the clinical presentation a breast primary is favored  To help exclude the possibility of metastasis from a different primary site  we performed a panel of immunoperoxidase stains on the core biopsy with the following results  Immunostain Target Result Vimentin Renal  mesenchymal cells Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Renal cell carcinoma Positive  weak focal staining  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  ovary Negative GCDFP 15 Breast Negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Negative TTF 1 Lung  thyroid Negative The immunoperoxidase staining pattern is indeterminate  Although a metastatic tumor cannot be excluded  the overall impression is that of a poorly differentiated carcinoma of the breast which has lost its immunoreactivity  Additional immunostains will be performed to help further classify the tumor and reported in an addendum  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL  COUNT  REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  0 2   SEE NOTE  Note  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 immunostained slides  LYMPH NODE  LEFT NON SENTINEL   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  0 2   SEE NOTE  Note  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 immunostained slides  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are three containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left axillary sentinel node   are two tan pink intact lymph nodes  which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serially sectioned  smaller lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serially sectioned  larger lymph node  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast core biopsy   are two tan yellow fibrofatty soft tissue cores averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  wrapped and submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  left axillary nonsentinel node   are two tan pink intact lymph nodes  which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The entire specimen is submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Bisected smaller lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Bisected larger lymph node  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  117  to chromosome 17 signals  111  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  3 Additional immunohistochemical stains were performed on the core biopsy to help clarify the origin of the tumor with the following results  Immunostain Target Result Cytokeratin Epithelial cells Positive Cytokeratin 19 Epithelial subset Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive  rare cells CDX 2 Gastrointestinal epithelium Negative The additional immunohistochemical staining pattern is indeterminate  Although a poorly differentiated breast carcinoma is favored  other tumors may express a similar profile  Although less likely  the differential based on the staining pattern includes renal cell carcinoma and pancreatic carcinoma  Clinical correlation and further evaluation are suggested  Addendum  3 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL  COUNT  REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT    CORE BIOPSY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT NON SENTINEL   EXCISION  report_end  , Negative.
